WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.502
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.736
How's everybody doing tonight?

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:04.737
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.239
Great to hear.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.508
In that case,
let's get to the news.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.478
First Lady Dr. Jill Biden
was heckled last week

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.512
outside of a Connecticut
ice cream shop,

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:18.484
but that's what you get
when you order rum raisin.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.887
West Virginia Senator
Joe Manchin announced today

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.189
that he's tested positive
for the coronavirus.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.760
Wow, he finally found something
he couldn't block.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.130
Former President Trump and
former Vice President Mike Pence

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.366
held competing rallies on Friday
in Arizona

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.336
so the chants were either,
"Run, Mike, run!"

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:40.206
Or "Run, Mike! Run!"

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.442
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:46.045
The annual Congressional
baseball game is scheduled

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.180
for Thursday evening
at Nationals Park,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.882
and oh, look at this,
Josh Hawley

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.751
is stealing third base.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.788
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:01.860
Newark, New Jersey -- in 1950.
He stole a base in 1950.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.599
There goes Hawley.
He's running down to third base.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.601
Newark, New Jersey, set a record
yesterday after reaching

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:13.005
its fifth day straight of
temperatures over 100 degrees.

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.942
It was so hot in New Jersey,
you could bake a ziti

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.376
on the sidewalk.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:21.180
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.716
That's a joke Johnny Carson
could have told,

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.653
except he couldn't, because when
Carson had this job,

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:30.256
it wasn't 100 degrees
five days in a row!

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:34.194
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.362
The New York Post
and The Wall Street Journal

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.030
each published an op ed
on Friday

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.232
denouncing former president
Trump for his role

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.434
in the Capitol attack,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.003
and USA Today
denounced him in a Garfield.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.208
Former Trump adviser
Steve Bannon was found guilty

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.845
last week of criminal contempt
of Congress and faces

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.480
up to two years in prison --

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.282
not including the two weeks
it takes to strip search him.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.184
All right, take off that shirt,
and then that other shirt,

00:01:59.184 --> 00:02:00.653
and then another one.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.788
Jesus, the layers on this guy."

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.423
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:07.126
And finally, the fast food chain
Subway will launch

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.162
a promotion this week that will
give customers free sandwiches

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:13.366
for a year if they get a tattoo
of the company's

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.968
Subway series logo
on their forearm.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.205
Meanwhile, Arby's will give you
a sandwich if you just write

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:23.409
"meat" on your forehead
with a sharpie.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.078
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

